ent-MedievalDoorUniversal = wooden door
    .desc = A lock can be attached to it.

ent-MedievalDoorReinforcedUniversal = reinforced door
    .desc = A lock can be attached to it.

construction-recipe-medieval-door-universal = wooden door
construction-recipe-medieval-door-universal-desc = A simple wooden door.

construction-recipe-medieval-door-reinforced-universal = reinforced wooden door
construction-recipe-medieval-door-reinforced-universal-desc = A sturdier wooden door reinforced for better protection.

construction-recipe-medieval-airlock-key = wooden door with lock
construction-recipe-medieval-airlock-key-desc = Craft a key to open it. Use the key on the handmade door once, while no other key is bound to it, to bind that key to the door. Further uses of the key will open or close the door. To make a duplicate, use a new key on the key whose access you wish to copy. One key can be bound to no more than one door.

ent-MedievalDoorKeySuperKey = divine key
    .desc = If you are reading this, give the key to the player with the ckey Zakvielian.

ent-MedievalDoorLockBase = door lock
    .desc = A lock for securing a door.

ent-MedievalDoorLockT1 = simple iron lock
    .desc = A simple lock. Press Z to set it up, then use it on a free door, chest, or anchor to attach it. To remove it, right-click the secured object and choose "Detach lock".

ent-MedievalDoorLockT2 = sturdy iron lock
    .desc = A sturdy lock. Press Z to set it up, then use it on a free door, chest, or anchor to attach it. To remove it, right-click the secured object and choose "Detach lock".

ent-MedievalDoorLockT3 = masterwork iron lock
    .desc = A masterwork lock. Press Z to set it up, then use it on a free door, chest, or anchor to attach it. To remove it, right-click the secured object and choose "Detach lock".

universal-security-eject-lock = Detach lock

